            "definition": "1. A royal city of the Canaanites, taken by Joshua and assigned to Issachar. Probably the same as the APHEKAH of Josh. 15:53. Josh. 12:18; I Sa. 4:1; 29:1. 2. A city of Asher, near Sidon; probably the same as APHIK. Josh. 19:30. 3. With the article, “the Aphek,” a place where the Philistines encamped while the Israelites were at Ebenezer. This was N. W. and not far from Jerusalem. It is now called Belled el-Foka. I Sa. 4:1. 4. In Issachar, the scene of a battle in which Saul was defeated by the Philistines. I Sa. 29:1. 5. A city E. of Cinneroth, and where Benhadad was defeated by Ahab. Now called Fik. I Ki. 20:26, 30; II Ki. 13:17."
